  "body": "Found during the theme audit for #2039 (checked on `upstream/main` `31f8d03d7`, and still present in open PR #2027).\n\nWhat happens:\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme.rs:76` defines `Tokens::font_caption: f32` (`12.5` in `DARK` and `LIGHT` at `:152` and `:194`), `theme.rs:346-347` validates it against `clamp::FONT`, and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme_files.rs:80,406` parses `\"font_caption\"` from theme JSON files.\n- At draw time, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/painted.rs:176` (`painted::caption`) formats ribbon group captions using `FontId::proportional(MIN_LABEL_PX)` (`10.0`, line 122) instead of `pal.font_caption`. Zero draw sites in `crates/ui/` read `font_caption`, so changing `font_caption` in a custom theme file (or `theme.json.example`) has no visual effect.\n\nExpected:\n- `painted::caption` reads `pal.font_caption` (clamped with `clamp::range(pal.font_caption, clamp::FONT)` or matching `font_label` scaling if a theme lowers it), or `Tokens::font_caption`'s built-in defaults (`12.5` vs `10.0`) are aligned so ribbon group captions reflect the theme setting without clipping against `ribbon_caption_row_h`.\n\nDone means:\n- `painted::caption` uses `pal.font_caption` instead of `MIN_LABEL_PX` (coordinate `Tokens::DARK`/`LIGHT` default value and `ribbon_rows` height checks if PR #2027 has merged).\n- A unit/UI test fails when `font_caption` is changed and `painted::caption` ignores it.\n",
